From bf6b2099d6351c37039b01447a9bb64f9a54a586 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: That in Rust <amul.exe@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:54:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: parse statement-position const closures as expressions

AI-assisted implementation; human review required before upstream submission. Base: 2a362a41a8eb6e090f1a12d9b712df85af6f0c33.

Mirrors rustc check_const_closure and parse_constness_: const closures must not be parsed as const items; stmt parsing falls through to expression parsing. Scope is move and pipe lookahead already supported by the expression parser.

rustc citation: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/58cf8f9c35b355199727627d07ae34a4e2846d67/compiler/rustc_parse/src/parser/mod.rs (check_const_closure, parse_constness_); expr.rs (parse_expr_closure); stmt.rs (parse_item_common fallback).

Co-Authored-By: Devin AI <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
